@startuml overview
' cumin-works - the states of an implementation issue in the merge stage.
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
' A transition is written: action [guard] / what cumin does. A gray state belongs to another area.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "reviewing" as Reviewing #EEEEEE
Reviewing : (the review area)

state "awaiting-merge-decision" as MergeDecision
MergeDecision : do / the Assignee reviews the pull request

state "merging" as Merging
Merging : do / cumin merges the pull request

state "implementing" as Implementing #EEEEEE
Implementing : (the implementation area)

state "checking" as Checking #EEEEEE
Checking : (the implementation area)

state "awaiting-blocker-merge" as AwaitingBase
AwaitingBase : no one works; the pull request of the blocker waits

state "awaiting-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Assignee answers

Reviewing --> Merging : start the merge\n[the review completed with APPROVE,\nthe required checks completed,\nthe risk is not in merge_decision_risks,\nno blocker to merge first (MERGE-003)]
Reviewing --> MergeDecision : ask for the merge decision\n[the same, but the risk is in merge_decision_risks]\n/ cumin asks the Assignee for a review, notifies
MergeDecision --> Merging : start the merge\n[the Assignee's APPROVE on the head commit,\nthe required checks completed]
MergeDecision --> Implementing : request an assignee review fix\n[the Assignee's REQUEST_CHANGES on the head commit,\nafter the last awaiting-merge-decision]\n/ cumin starts the Implementer in the same session
Reviewing --> AwaitingBase : wait for the blocker merge (MERGE-013)\n[the same, but the base is not main,\nor a blocker is open]
AwaitingBase --> Implementing : take in the main branch and check again\n(the implementation area, IMPL-008.5)
AwaitingBase --> Decision : stop (the implementation area, IMPL-008.6)
Merging --> Merging : merge\n[not merged, the merge conditions hold, no conflict]\n/ cumin merges the approved commit
Merging --> [*] : close the merged issue\n[merged]\n/ cumin closes the issue if GitHub did not
Merging --> Checking : go back to the checks\n[not merged, a merge condition fails]
Merging --> Implementing : request a conflict resolution\n[the merge conditions hold, a conflict]\n/ cumin starts the Implementer in the same session
Merging --> Decision : stop the merge\n[the merge was refused for another reason,\nor the issue cannot be closed]\n/ cumin comments, notifies

@enduml
